PROJECT: Stratagem AI — Enterprise Decision Intelligence & Strategic Knowledge Discovery Platform.
EXECUTION MODE: Autonomous End-to-End Production Build (Zero Placeholders, Zero Mock Data Bypass, Full Type & Schema Safety).
You are tasked with architecting, implementing, validating, and shipping Stratagem AI, a full-stack AI-powered Decision Intelligence web application. You write clean, modular, strictly validated, production-grade code. You never leave // TODO comments, stubbed functions, or incomplete UI views. Every database table, API endpoint, Zod validator, Gemini structured-output call, and React visual component must be wired end to end.

2. Core Mission Directive
Organizations and individuals routinely fail to make timely, optimal decisions because critical context is fragmented across qualitative constraints, quantitative metrics, hidden risks, and competing stakeholder priorities.

Your mission is to build a full-stack Decision Intelligence & Research Discovery Platform that transforms ambiguous real-world dilemmas into structured, auditable, data-driven decisions. The platform must ingest decision contexts, constraints, criteria weights, and candidate alternatives; execute multi-dimensional AI trade-off analysis using the official Google Gemini SDK (@google/genai); evaluate risk exposure and sensitivity scenarios; and render explainable, visually interactive recommendations with side-by-side radar, bar, and risk-matrix charts.

3. Product Goal
Deliver a complete, deployable, multi-tenant web application (Stratagem AI) that enables users to:

Define complex real-world decision problems across strategic domains (Enterprise Architecture, Capital Allocation, Product Strategy, Supply Chain & Operations, Career & Talent, Public Policy & ESG).

Configure weighted evaluation criteria, hard constraints, budget/time ceilings, risk tolerance, and 2 to 6 competing options/alternatives.

Trigger an AI Decision Intelligence Engine powered by Google Gemini (gemini-2.5-flash) that performs:

Multi-Criteria Decision Analysis (MCDA) with normalized scoring (0–100) across every option and criterion.

Pattern & Trade-off Discovery identifying non-obvious synergies, bottlenecks, and second-order effects.

Probabilistic Risk Assessment categorizing risks by likelihood, impact severity, and actionable mitigation strategies.

Scenario Sensitivity Stress-Testing (Best Case, Base Case, Worst Case / Black Swan shock).

Explainable Recommendation Synthesis with transparent reasoning, confidence intervals, and an actionable 30-60-90 day execution roadmap.

Persist, compare, filter, bookmark, and export past decision workspaces and run interactive "What-If" follow-up simulations via an embedded AI Decision Copilot.

4. Mandatory Features
JWT + bcrypt Authentication & Workspace Isolation: Full user registration, login, session persistence, token refresh/validation middleware, and strict per-user data isolation.

Guided Multi-Step Decision Builder: Dynamic form wizard allowing users to select a domain, define the decision problem, add custom weighted criteria (auto-normalized or validated), input multiple candidate alternatives with pros/cons/estimated costs, and set risk appetite.

AI Decision Intelligence Engine: Server-side integration with @google/genai enforcing strict JSON Schema outputs for deterministic rendering of scores, trade-offs, risk matrices, and explainable rationales.

Interactive Visual Analytics Dashboard (Recharts):

Multi-Option Radar Chart: Comparing alternatives across key evaluation dimensions (Cost Efficiency, Strategic Alignment, Speed to Value, Risk Resilience, Scalability).

Weighted Score Stacked/Grouped Bar Chart: Visualizing total weighted utility scores per alternative.

Risk Exposure Scatter / Heatmap Matrix: Plotting identified risks by Likelihood (1–5) vs. Severity Impact (1–5).

Scenario Sensitivity Comparison Chart: Comparing alternative performance under Base, Optimistic, and Stress-Test scenarios.

Explainable AI (XAI) Audit Trail: Clear breakdown of why the winning option was selected, explicit trade-offs accepted, key assumptions made, and conditions under which the recommendation would flip (reversal triggers).

Interactive "What-If" Simulation Copilot: Contextual chat & parameter perturbation drawer inside each decision report allowing users to ask follow-up questions (e.g., "What if our budget drops by 30% and timeline shrinks to 3 months?") and persist the conversation history.

Decision Knowledge Library & Search: Filterable, searchable repository of all user decisions by domain, status, confidence score, and date, plus one-click sample decision templates for instant demo testing.

Submission & Export Ready: Printable / Markdown-exportable Executive Decision Memo for stakeholder alignment.

