7. User Flow
Onboarding & Authentication:

User visits / → clicks Get Started or Try Live Demo → registers at /register or logs in at /login → backend verifies credentials, issues a signed JWT (7d expiry), and redirects to /dashboard.

Decision Framing & Input Capture:

User clicks + New Decision Analysis (/decisions/new).

User either selects one of 4 pre-built rich real-world scenarios (for instant evaluation) OR completes the 4-part structured form:

Step 1: Title, Domain Category, Decision Urgency, and Problem Context/Background.

Step 2: Hard Constraints (Budget ceiling, Timeline deadline, Regulatory/Technical non-negotiables) & Risk Appetite (Conservative, Balanced, Aggressive).

Step 3: Evaluation Criteria (e.g., Total Cost of Ownership, Time-to-Market, Scalability, Risk Exposure, Strategic Fit) with importance weights (1–10).

Step 4: Candidate Alternatives (minimum 2, up to 6 options) with description, estimated cost, estimated timeline, and known pros/cons.

AI Analysis Execution:

User submits the decision payload → Backend validates payload with Zod → Saves raw decision & options in PostgreSQL within a transaction → Invokes Gemini (gemini-2.5-flash) with structured JSON Schema → Validates AI output with Zod → Persists structured report, option scores, risk matrix, and sensitivity scenarios in PostgreSQL → Returns complete payload to Frontend.

Interactive Exploration & What-If Simulation:

User is routed to /decisions/:id → Explores the winning recommendation, confidence score, Recharts Radar & Bar charts, Risk Matrix, and Reversal Triggers.

User opens the What-If Simulation Copilot panel → Submits a perturbation query → Backend fetches the full decision context + prior report, queries Gemini for a quantitative sensitivity re-evaluation, saves the interaction, and updates the UI in real time.

