18. Security Requirements
Password Security: Hash all passwords with bcryptjs using 12 salt rounds. Never return password_hash in any API response.

JWT Authentication: Sign tokens with process.env.JWT_SECRET and set expiration (expiresIn: "7d"). Verify tokens in server/middleware/authMiddleware.js via the Authorization: Bearer <token> header.

API Key Protection: GEMINI_API_KEY and DATABASE_URL must reside strictly on the server. Add .env to .gitignore.

Rate Limiting: Apply express-rate-limit on /api/auth/* (20 requests / 15 min) and /api/decisions/analyze (30 requests / hour) to prevent abuse and quota exhaustion.

HTTP Hardening: Enable helmet() for secure HTTP headers and configure cors() to allow process.env.CLIENT_URL (and localhost during development).

SQL Injection Prevention: Use exclusively parameterized queries ($1, $2, ...) with pg.Pool. String concatenation in SQL queries is strictly forbidden.

